## Summary

Shipped a production-polished, Apple-idiomatic **`WidgetSettingsModal`** SwiftUI surface at parity with `web/src/features/dashboard/components/WidgetSettingsModal.tsx`, following the repo's established `AdvancedSettings`/`ToolCard` conventions.

**Delivered** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/`, 11 files, ~1.6k LOC):
- **Parity**: section gating (`isVehicleWidget`/`isChartWidget`), vehicle/refresh/time-range selects + show-title toggle, the `display_name || "Vehicle <id>"` fallback, and the controlled `setConfig` transforms (`'all'`/`'default'`→nil, timeRange, showTitle) reproduced verbatim, with config passthrough preserved on save.
- **Architecture**: pure Foundation projector + reducer; `@Observable @MainActor` model binding `useVehicles` through a P1/S8 vehicles **Store seam** (no HTTP in the view); P1/S10 surface-table i18n facade; P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry seam.
- **All states render** (never blank): loading / ready / empty / error+retry / stale (chip + one auto-refresh) / offline (cached + chip).
- **a11y**: VoiceOver labels on every control + per-phase summaries; Dynamic Type; Reduce-Motion safe.
- Presented as `NavigationStack` sheet content (native focus-trap + dismiss) with toolbar Cancel + web-footer Cancel/Save.

